# apt.list — Debian / Ubuntu / Mint baseline (server + CLI).
# One package per line; blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped.
# setup.sh runs `sudo apt install -y` on every non-comment line.
#
# Desktop additions live in apt-desktop.list. Packages absent from apt
# repos (starship, atuin, rustup, lefthook, tealdeer, bandwhich, ghostty,
# discord, veracrypt, JetBrains Mono Nerd Font) fall through to either
# snap.list or a release-binary bootstrap in setup.sh.
#
# Source of truth for the apt column of doc/packages-native.md. Keep
# the two in lockstep (CLAUDE.md §6).

# Shell + prompt
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-syntax-highlighting

# File / search tools
eza
bat
fzf
ripgrep
fd-find
zoxide
tealdeer
jq

# Editor stack
vim
neovim
tmux

# Git + dev tooling
git
git-delta
gnupg
pinentry-curses
shellcheck

# Language toolchains
golang-go
nodejs
llvm
clang-format
clang-tidy
# Rust LSP — apt 22.04+ / Debian 12+. Older releases: fall through to
# `rustup component add rust-analyzer` (handled in setup.sh).
rust-analyzer
# Faster linker for Rust ELF builds. apt 22.10+ / Debian 12+; older
# releases skip it without error (setup.sh logs and continues).
mold

# Networking / sysadmin
arp-scan
dnsutils
wget
curl

# Containers — left commented because Docker on Linux is per-user choice
# (rooted via systemd / rootless via dockerd-rootless / Docker Desktop /
# colima / k3d), and the wrong combination causes dpkg file-conflict
# errors. Uncomment the variant you want:
#
# (a) Rooted, Debian-packaged (system daemon, requires sudo):
# docker.io
# docker-buildx
#
# (b) Rooted via Docker's official APT repo (download.docker.com — needs
#     repo setup first; see https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/debian/):
# docker-ce
# docker-ce-cli
# containerd.io
# docker-buildx-plugin
# docker-compose-plugin
#
# (c) Rootless (CLI + rootless extras from Docker's official APT repo,
#     no system daemon — pair with `dockerd-rootless-setuptool.sh install`):
# docker-ce-cli
# docker-ce-rootless-extras
# docker-buildx-plugin
# docker-compose-plugin

# VM / virtualization (comment out if you don't need libvirt/qemu)
libvirt-daemon-system
qemu-system

# Filesystem / misc
sqlite3
zip
unzip
asciinema

# Fonts
fonts-font-awesome
fonts-jetbrains-mono
